[{"answer":"Today we're going to look at one of my favourite fish -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/1.mp3"},{"answer":"the shark.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/2.mp3"},{"answer":"As you know, sharks have a reputation for being very dangerous creatures","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/3.mp3"},{"answer":"capable of injuring or killing humans,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/4.mp3"},{"answer":"and I'd like to talk about sharks in Australia.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/5.mp3"},{"answer":"Sharks are rather large fish,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/6.mp3"},{"answer":"often growing to over 10 metres","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/7.mp3"},{"answer":"and the longest sharks caught in Australia have reached sixteen metres.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/8.mp3"},{"answer":"Sharks vary in weight with size and breed, of course,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/9.mp3"},{"answer":"but the heaviest shark caught in Australia was a White Pointer -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/10.mp3"},{"answer":"that weighed 795 kilograms -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/11.mp3"},{"answer":"quite a size!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/12.mp3"},{"answer":"Sharks have a different structure to most fish:","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/13.mp3"},{"answer":"instead of a skeleton made of bone,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/14.mp3"},{"answer":"they have a tough elastic skeleton of cartilage.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/15.mp3"},{"answer":"Unlike bone, this firm, pliable material is rather like your nose,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/16.mp3"},{"answer":"and allows the shark to bend easily as it swims.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/17.mp3"},{"answer":"The shark's skin isn't covered with scales, like other fish,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/18.mp3"},{"answer":"instead, the skin's covered with barbs, giving it a rough texture like sandpaper.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/19.mp3"},{"answer":"As you know, sharks are very quick swimmers.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/20.mp3"},{"answer":"This is made possible by their fins,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/21.mp3"},{"answer":"one set at the side and another set underneath the body,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/22.mp3"},{"answer":"and the tail also helps the shark move forward quickly.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/23.mp3"},{"answer":"Unlike other fish,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/24.mp3"},{"answer":"sharks have to keep swimming if they want to stay at a particular depth,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/25.mp3"},{"answer":"and they rarely swim at the surface.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/26.mp3"},{"answer":"Mostly, they swim at the bottom of the ocean,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/27.mp3"},{"answer":"scavenging and picking up food that's lying on the ocean floor.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/28.mp3"},{"answer":"While most other animals, including fish, hunt their prey by means of their eyesight,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/29.mp3"},{"answer":"sharks hunt essentially by smell.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/30.mp3"},{"answer":"They have a very acute sense of smell -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/31.mp3"},{"answer":"and can sense the presence of food long before they can see it.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/32.mp3"},{"answer":"In Australia, where people spend a lot of time at the beach,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/33.mp3"},{"answer":"the government has realised that it must prevent sharks from swimming near its beaches.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/34.mp3"},{"answer":"As a result, they've introduced a beach-netting program.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/35.mp3"},{"answer":"Beach-netting, or meshing, involves setting large nets parallel to the shore;","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/36.mp3"},{"answer":"this means that the nets on New South Wales beaches are set on one day,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/37.mp3"},{"answer":"and then lifted and taken out to sea on the next day.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/38.mp3"},{"answer":"When shark-netting first began in 1939,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/39.mp3"},{"answer":"only the Sydney metropolitan beaches were meshed -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/40.mp3"},{"answer":"these beaches were chosen because beaches near the city are usually the most crowded with swimmers.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/41.mp3"},{"answer":"Ten years later, in 1949,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/42.mp3"},{"answer":"systematic meshing was extended to include the beaches to the south of Sydney.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/43.mp3"},{"answer":"As a result of the general success of the program in Sydney,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/44.mp3"},{"answer":"shark-meshing was introduced to the state of Queensland around 1970.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/45.mp3"},{"answer":"The New Zealand authorities also looked at it,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/46.mp3"},{"answer":"but considered meshing uneconomical - as did Tahiti in the Pacific.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/47.mp3"},{"answer":"At around the same time, South Africa introduced meshing to some of its most popular swimming beaches.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/48.mp3"},{"answer":"When meshing began, approximately 1500 sharks were caught in the first year.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/49.mp3"},{"answer":"However, this declined in the years that followed,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/50.mp3"},{"answer":"and since that time, the average annual catch has been only about 150 a year.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/51.mp3"},{"answer":"The majority of sharks are caught during the warmest months, from November to February,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/52.mp3"},{"answer":"when sharks are most active","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/53.mp3"},{"answer":"and when both the air and the ocean are at their maximum temperature.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/54.mp3"},{"answer":"Despite quite large catches,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/55.mp3"},{"answer":"some people believe that shark meshing is not the best way to catch sharks.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/56.mp3"},{"answer":"It's not that they think sharks are afraid of nets, or because they eat holes in them,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/57.mp3"},{"answer":"because neither of these is true.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/58.mp3"},{"answer":"But meshing does appear to be less effective than some other methods,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/59.mp3"},{"answer":"especially when there are big seas with high rolling waves and strong currents","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/60.mp3"},{"answer":"and anything that lets the sand move -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/61.mp3"},{"answer":"the sand that's holding the nets down.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/62.mp3"},{"answer":"When this moves the nets will also become less effective.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-4-test-4-part-4-2023-08-13-18-11-18/63.mp3"}]
